# UI / UX Rule

Reference:
- `docs/00-input/ui-reference/ui-reference-01.png`
- `wireframes/WIREFRAME-SPEC.md`
- `docs/v0.2/SCREEN-CATALOG.md`

Principles:
- The image reference communicates visual direction; do not clone it 1:1.
- User Portal: content-first, visual, large module entry points, responsive.
- Admin Portal: operational, sidebar/table/form/dashboard oriented.
- Home must expose all 9 main modules.
- Desktop target: clear 3-column module grid where space allows.
- Mobile target: 1–2 columns depending on width.
- Keep content hierarchy readable over decorative backgrounds.
- Avoid excessive gradients, shadows, animation, or ornamental detail.
- Do not invent a final design token system before `docs/v0.5/UI-GUIDELINE.md` is approved.
- For the UI-report milestone, mock interactions are allowed only when clearly isolated from production data behavior.
